{"title":"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Picture_for_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Picture for Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Vectors)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Vectors)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square piece of paper has sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. From each corner a wedge is cut in the following manner: at each corner, the two cuts for the wedge each start at a distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a6847786e6937f02f810e74a056f4c8f289a931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> from the corner, and they meet on the diagonal at an angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> (see the figure below). The paper is then folded up along the lines joining the vertices of adjacent cuts. When the two edges of a cut meet, they are taped together. The result is a paper tray whose sides are not at right angles to the base. The height of the tray, that is, the perpendicular distance between the plane of the base and the plane formed by the upper edges, can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf14ec08d1380e317bdbb9e0ebeaa4ed75f72c17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[n]{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aae65ae74048caadfc0962cc6a29cebd3f1dc100.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&lt;1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th power of any prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/21378bf620713fc38bd4747453f6451f9faf16bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]import cse5; size(200); pathpen=black; real s=sqrt(17); real r=(sqrt(51)+s)/sqrt(2); D((0,2*s)--(0,0)--(2*s,0)); D((0,s)--r*dir(45)--(s,0)); D((0,0)--r*dir(45)); D((r*dir(45).x,2*s)--r*dir(45)--(2*s,r*dir(45).y)); MP(&quot;30^\\circ&quot;,r*dir(45)-(0.25,1),SW); MP(&quot;30^\\circ&quot;,r*dir(45)-(1,0.5),SW); MP(&quot;\\sqrt{17}&quot;,(0,s/2),W); MP(&quot;\\sqrt{17}&quot;,(s/2,0),S); MP(&quot;\\mathrm{cut}&quot;,((0,s)+r*dir(45))/2,N); MP(&quot;\\mathrm{cut}&quot;,((s,0)+r*dir(45))/2,E); MP(&quot;\\mathrm{fold}&quot;,(r*dir(45).x,s+r/2*dir(45).y),E); MP(&quot;\\mathrm{fold}&quot;,(s+r/2*dir(45).x,r*dir(45).y));[/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"322\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Picture_for_Solutions\">Picture for Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Picture for Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(Used for the following solutions)\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/8/2b89265cc1c5661571a60771a16c9caad4c4caa4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import three; import math; import cse5; import olympiad; size(500); pathpen=blue; real r = (51^0.5-17^0.5)/200, h=867^0.25/100; triple A=(0,0,0),B=(1,0,0),C=(1,1,0),D=(0,1,0); triple F=B+(r,-r,h),G=(1,-r,h),H=(1+r,0,h),I=B+(0,0,h); draw(B--F--H--cycle); draw(B--F--G--cycle); draw(G--I--H); draw(B--I); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); triple Fa=A+(-r,-r, h), Fc=C+(r,r, h), Fd=D+(-r,r, h); triple Ia = A+(0,0,h), Ic = C+(0,0,h), Id = D+(0,0,h); draw(Ia--I--Ic); draw(Fa--F--Fc--Fd--cycle); draw(A--Fa); draw(C--Fc); draw(D--Fd); triple A1 = (F.x,F.y,0); real factor = 1/4; draw(F--A1--B); draw((A1+(F-A1)*factor)--(A1+(F-A1)*factor+(B-A1)*factor)--(A1+(B-A1)*factor));  [/asy]\" width=\"835\" height=\"302\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the original picture, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the corner, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the two points whose distance is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a6847786e6937f02f810e74a056f4c8f289a931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Also, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the point where the two cuts intersect.\n</p><p>Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/5641c1daf0b5098e68f5bb5524af0b5ce999b0d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{MNP}$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> (a 45-45-90 triangle), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db9b9034ae260ac37a15b41ccd24acc68a269011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN=MP\\sqrt{2}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad MN=\\sqrt{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"285\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5ae85e1048e14a30e503434955ce2709629f0a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{MNR}$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equilateral_triangle\" title=\"Equilateral triangle\">equilateral</a>, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/fee869a2a663c20babd5261ef68072fb3af22954.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MR = NR = \\sqrt{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />. (Alternatively, we could find this by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">Law of Sines</a>.)\n</p><p>The length of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/5641c1daf0b5098e68f5bb5524af0b5ce999b0d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{MNP}$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/2/95266e2accffb5f44568ee179e580091df365b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"35\" height=\"45\" />, and the length of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5ae85e1048e14a30e503434955ce2709629f0a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{MNR}$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9beddea1f20b8eceb23b81a2ca318b618092526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{51}}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"35\" height=\"45\" />. Adding those two lengths, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e71c8680eb680eb22bd6bd6a6c121780782410e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR=\\frac{\\sqrt{17}+\\sqrt{51}}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"143\" height=\"45\" />. (Alternatively, we could have used that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8e5f70275d32d8dd2b955a46d39b1bada09ce47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 75^{\\circ} = \\sin (30+45) = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"268\" height=\"41\" />.)\n</p><p>Drop a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendicular</a> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the side of the square containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and let the intersection be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/193429ead30bc32f85360899ab16c27d2070f56f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}PG&amp;=\\frac{PR}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{17}+\\sqrt{51}}{2}\\\\ MG=PG-PM&amp;=\\frac{\\sqrt{17}+\\sqrt{51}}{2}-\\sqrt{17}=\\frac{\\sqrt{51}-\\sqrt{17}}{2}\\end{align*}\" width=\"430\" height=\"93\" />\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d1876820ecbfcf6cfb1b201e8d429431680538.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]import cse5; size(200); pathpen=black; real s=sqrt(17), r=(sqrt(51)+s)/(sqrt(2)); pair P=(0,0), N=(0,sqrt(17)), M=(sqrt(17),0), R=r*dir(45), G=((sqrt(51)+sqrt(17))/2,0); D(2*N--P--2*M); D(N--R--M); D(P--R); D((R.x,2*N.y)--R--(2*M.x,R.y)); MP(&quot;30^\\circ&quot;,R-(0.25,1),SW); MP(&quot;30^\\circ&quot;,R-(1,0.5),SW); MP(&quot;\\sqrt{17}&quot;,N/2,W); MP(&quot;\\sqrt{17}&quot;,M/2,S); D(N--M,dashed); D(G--R,dashed); MP(&quot;P&quot;,P,SW); MP(&quot;N&quot;,N,SW); MP(&quot;M&quot;,M,SW); MP(&quot;R&quot;,R,NE); MP(&quot;G&quot;,G,SW); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"322\" /></center>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4aa4d85335863f762ae4128b05ede6d4e918678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;D&#39;$\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> be the smaller square base of the tray and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be the larger square, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d59f5d75cc27d504ede022aab803742e799709f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA&#39;$\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, etc, are edges. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4aa4d85335863f762ae4128b05ede6d4e918678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;D&#39;$\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7e8b00cecea70dec4019ff67896ee423713fe26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA&#39;=MR=\\sqrt{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a29ef5981c2d979c113ca57ca185badbd83f9f1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;F=MG\\sqrt{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{51}-\\sqrt{17}}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"234\" height=\"48\" />. Now, use the Pythagorean Theorem on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/156a97ec178b1693abe7dda10640b7ca83d43d04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFA&#39;$\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a7d82d09afe83998acd18d8f16ff981f6f75ee1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{51}-\\sqrt{17}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^2+AF^2&amp;=\\left(\\sqrt{34}\\right)^2\\\\ \\frac{51-34\\sqrt{3}+17}{2}+AF^2&amp;=34\\\\AF&amp;=\\sqrt{34-\\frac{68-34\\sqrt{3}}{2}}\\\\AF&amp;=\\sqrt{\\frac{34\\sqrt{3}}{2}}\\\\AF&amp;=\\sqrt[4]{867}\\end{align*}\" width=\"352\" height=\"251\" />\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/a/a9a0522b89e364c7ea033881c6d3bb3893497215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$867 + 4 = \\boxed{871}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the final pyramid, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be the smaller square and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4aa4d85335863f762ae4128b05ede6d4e918678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;D&#39;$\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> be the larger square such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d59f5d75cc27d504ede022aab803742e799709f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA&#39;$\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, etc. are edges.\n</p><p>It is obvious from the diagram that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f75b76ae0a7d47d205782f10a2125fb6ef0b8e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A&#39;AB = \\angle A&#39;AD = 105^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"201\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> axes in a 3-d coordinate system such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> has a positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> coordinate. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the angle made with the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Axis\" title=\"Axis\">axis</a>. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> analogously.\n</p><p>It is easy to see that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/6/136ec6cde9dbc53f0cbaf9e1a9ce15e452fe9799.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P: = (x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/3/8d3da1654e06f75af1712d9e7f0c1af07ff7bc4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = AA&#39;\\cdot \\cos\\alpha$\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />. Furthermore, this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/665a6e354cf4df94661de3369454f2a21472c98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {x^2}{AA&#39;^2} + \\frac {y^2}{AA&#39;^2} + \\frac {z^2}{AA&#39;^2} = \\cos^2\\alpha + \\cos^2\\beta + \\cos^2\\gamma = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"411\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f92f9d4985f4baf35cc0821d8a309d2291dc55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha = \\beta = 105^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb52d85feb06816f6bbf27555bf77bc9aa601fad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^2 105^\\circ + \\cos^2105^\\circ + \\cos^2\\gamma = 1\\implies \\cos\\gamma = \\sqrt [4]{\\frac {3}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"406\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>It is easy to see from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">Law of Sines</a> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb1be0d80664a8926a7e4d77951a73234ae801d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {AA&#39;}{\\sin 45^\\circ} = \\frac {\\sqrt {17}}{\\sin 30^\\circ}\\implies AA&#39; = \\sqrt {34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"274\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/ded368c8527319aae743e234756d997afbe06179.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = AA&#39;\\cdot \\cos\\gamma = \\sqrt [4]{34^2\\cdot \\frac {3}{4}} = \\sqrt [4]{867}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"278\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>It follows that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/a/a9a0522b89e364c7ea033881c6d3bb3893497215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$867 + 4 = \\boxed{871}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" />.~Shen Kislay Kai\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Vectors.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Vectors)\">Solution 3 (Vectors)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Vectors)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a corner of the square. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the points where the cuts start from the edges, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the point where the cuts meet. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be points such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/04292549d378ac933969018243d991d23fab6950.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OX=OY=1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84b02fe16202f26f1711ecbf8f690a10d319eb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{OX} \\parallel \\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/f/19facf22722c1aae8d7fd08d2d471812262c73f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{OY} \\parallel \\overline{AC},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"22\" /> respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the point such that the cuts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0964c9cf406ef8e5ec8beaa6a92125f2d8f90460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> when folded. \n</p><p>By the AAS congruence theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1ea05bfa4948cc97b775536e3f1025e0419be5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AOC} \\cong \\triangle{AOB}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" /> Hence, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a9776cddadd5f2e0bb9076743b743935eef7e1d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{OBC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is equilateral and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/6542ff98a0a3b3da3abbe238b37b5067a48a76ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB=OC=BC=OP.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"193\" height=\"14\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is an isosceles right triangle, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b50c93127c4c5efe268c7abcc6d76316ecb3f09f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP=OB=OC=BC=AB\\cdot\\sqrt{2}=\\sqrt{17}\\cdot\\sqrt{2}=\\sqrt{34}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"437\" height=\"21\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83a974fa2b1dbf0b77ec5f584367f2ac4466519d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP=\\sqrt{34}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Also, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/1/a91799cc10cba56e2e7a1c00306b39f3b16d4066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{POX}=\\angle{BOX}=\\angle{AOX}-\\angle{AOB}=105^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"366\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Furthermore, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917f191ee61209a4958553a422b0e47289266459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O=(0,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" /> be the origin, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/5/c7586d25ce02d44a601db5eb9165e1f5ff82d0a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X=(1,0,0),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75df2bb7f13629f9adc16ac6d6989ea668f157b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y=(0,1,0).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"20\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c38267158f261458215064adc65afc9d638afa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{P}=\\begin{pmatrix} p_1 \\\\ p_2 \\\\ p_3 \\end{pmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -28px\" width=\"92\" height=\"66\" /> denote the vector at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/ede78a06018011f48c24a76284afce482ebc6c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/41412724806cedc4746cc38e34f2c2bc977e93da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{X}=\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -28px\" width=\"84\" height=\"66\" /> denote the vector at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/098eec17ab0e016beced75c6895f17c4edb1bcc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"19\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/f/3ef38d5c1c32bbc99832c01a78119f7e47bb8650.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{Y}=\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -28px\" width=\"84\" height=\"66\" /> denote the vector at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/51699aeac52c7ea992acf29d1e92aadd5017be2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> It suffices to solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/4079cc02fbfd3f4ccc7664891083e7d5d5269f53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"21\" height=\"11\" />\n</p><p>By the properties of the dot product for vectors, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5aecfe563c87299c38dd771cf6c98b3c2367b4d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overrightarrow{P}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{X}=\\overrightarrow{P}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{Y}=\\|\\overrightarrow{P}\\|\\|\\overrightarrow{X}\\|\\cos\\angle{POX}=\\|\\overrightarrow{P}\\|\\|\\overrightarrow{Y}\\|\\cos\\angle{POY}.\\]\" width=\"495\" height=\"26\" /> \nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/8/518c0048271d633e79a3e4ac5a7038731f9c51e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{POX}=\\angle{POY}=105^\\circ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/4/c3495ec4b18fb30ec71313d7d5b9cabbc010aa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\|\\overrightarrow{P}\\|=OP=\\sqrt{34},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"25\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd7a7336c8c7719e079330dc244230eb6b03a8bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\|\\overrightarrow{X}\\|=\\|\\overrightarrow{Y}\\|=1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"25\" /> the above equations simplify to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/1/3614d589eea03a763d95e3a380dcd671b2154f6d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{pmatrix} p_1 \\\\ p_2 \\\\ p_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\cdot\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix} p_1 \\\\ p_2 \\\\ p_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\cdot\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}=\\sqrt{34}\\cos 105^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"347\" height=\"64\" />\nThis leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/2/712e0c8058096f1f33d2a2cec50206ccc8a62361.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1=p_2=\\sqrt{34}\\cos 105^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"23\" /> Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/9/72947906786b7a1b18f6d84384bc7393a38b40e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\|\\overrightarrow{P}\\|=\\sqrt{34},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"25\" /> we have \n\\begin{align*}\np_3^2&amp;=34-(p_1^2+p_2^2)\\\\\n&amp;=34-2\\cdot(\\sqrt{34}\\cos 105^\\circ)^2\\\\\n&amp;=34(1-2\\cos^2 105^\\circ)\\\\\n&amp;=-34\\cos 210^\\circ\\\\\n&amp;=34\\cos 30^\\circ\\\\\n&amp;=34\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\\n&amp;=17\\sqrt{3}\\\\\n&amp;=\\sqrt{867}.\\\\\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/d/17dc464a33ffa852b2bbfe178a04c1878623f0ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_3=\\sqrt[4]{867}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"23\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/e/6febe2642519bf419bff896403dcb00e7f30658a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=\\boxed{871}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"119\" height=\"25\" /> \n</p><p>~ReticulatedPython\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I\" title=\"2008 AIME I\">2008 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2008\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017155431\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.054 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.074 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 636/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1757/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 116/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 22733/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.301      1 -total\n 58.86%    7.240     